WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.833
- You have a seven year
old, I have a seven...

00:00:01.833 --> 00:00:03.230
I have a five and seven
year old actually at home,

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.063
but you have a seven year old.

00:00:04.063 --> 00:00:05.160
So how are you enjoying fatherhood?

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.080
Do you love it?

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.970
- I really do, I love it.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.850
Because, it... this kid was
a blessing to God for me,

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.570
I'm telling you, because
we weren't expecting him,

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.360
he pops up and he is
everything that I was as a kid.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:18.550
So every time I hug him,
every time I say I love you,

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:19.830
every time I'm correcting him,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.620
or chastising him in love,

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.453
I'm healing myself in
some part of my childhood.

00:00:24.453 --> 00:00:26.410
So it's so beautiful to have him

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:28.150
and he's such a great, great kid.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.680
And we've kept him off social
media, kept him off of iPads,

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.600
all the other stuff, so that
he can find out who he is

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:34.480
before the world starts trying to tell him

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.710
that he's my son or he's somebody else.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:37.707
- That's powerful.
- [Tyler] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:37.707 --> 00:00:39.016
(audience applauds)

00:00:39.016 --> 00:00:40.950
- We do this, I don't allow
my kids to have the...

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.040
I'm like, I'm sorry, you're
probably not gonna have it

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:43.873
while you're in my household.

00:00:43.873 --> 00:00:45.350
I'm just like, 'cause it's scary.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.030
- Because I watched it whenever I,

00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:48.790
I was married, we had two older kids

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:50.980
and I watched these teenagers like,

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.477
be validated by likes or if
they didn't get likes they're,

00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:54.680
"Oh, I guess I'll take this picture down."

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.580
I'm like, wait, what?

00:00:55.580 --> 00:00:57.960
I'm like, don't let somebody, you know,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.540
control like your power or
have your power like that.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.460
- Like, it's a scary thing
and I think it's just still,

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.220
we haven't quite figured
it out until that happened.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:07.710
Sorry, you're not getting it.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.130
- Yeah, until the Congress steps in,

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.290
there's some sort of regulations

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.495
to what's happening right now,

00:01:11.495 --> 00:01:12.328
I don't know if we're
ever gonna get better.

00:01:12.328 --> 00:01:15.720
- I mean the bullying, the
suicide rates, like it's crazy.

00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:16.650
Speaking of suicide rates,

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:17.560
I don't wanna bring the show down

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.600
but I am seeing things
I have never seen before

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:21.930
with people just committing suicide.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.880
I'm like what is going on in the world?

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.490
But if you look at the state of the world

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:26.750
and everything that's happening,

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:28.690
people will start to think
that there's no hope,

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:30.230
but I'm here to tell you there is.

00:01:30.230 --> 00:01:31.063
- Absolutely.
- There is tremendous hope.

00:01:31.063 --> 00:01:32.520
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.980
You have to hold onto it.

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:34.813
Gotta hold onto it.

00:01:34.813 --> 00:01:36.450
- Yeah, and it's how you filter your day

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.620
of what you're taking in.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:39.542
- Yes, filter it, filter it.

00:01:39.542 --> 00:01:40.730
- You know you should
read The Tipping Point

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:41.690
if you haven't already.
- I haven't, I haven't.

00:01:41.690 --> 00:01:42.960
- It's really good, but it discusses...

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:44.180
Anyway, I'll talk about that later.

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:46.573
Um, anyway, but a lot of
people write into the show

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:47.910
with parenting questions,

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.590
so we thought that it might be fun

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:51.120
for Tyler and I to answer some of those.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.500
Maybe we'll fail, we don't know.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.470
Um, are you cool with it?

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:54.332
You don't have a choice.

00:01:54.332 --> 00:01:55.490
- Okay, good.
(both laugh)

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:56.990
- I was just wondering if I'm gonna answer

00:01:56.990 --> 00:01:58.950
as Tyler or Medea, but we'll
go ahead, we'll figure it out.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:01.170
- You can... either one can answer.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:03.430
- I'm excited at the
opportunity of either one.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:04.770
Okay, so let's see the first one.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:09.770
So, how do you deal with
having to watch (laughs)

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.980
the same movie or hear the
same song 27 times in a row?

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.190
- When your kid's very young,
how'd you deal with it?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.520
- My kids still do it!

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:18.353
Five and seven, they still...

00:02:18.353 --> 00:02:20.900
I've seen Encanto, I
love Encanto, luckily.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.270
Thank you Encanto people.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:24.680
But like it, but I
have... I can recite it.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.755
- [Tyler] Yeah.
- Yep.

00:02:25.755 --> 00:02:27.780
- And then we get in the
car and I'm not allowed to

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.510
play anything else other
than the soundtrack.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.000
- And you... and you're okay?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.290
- I'm okay, I can compartmentalize.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:34.190
It's crazy.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.660
- That's good that you
can compartmentalize

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:36.736
but I'm gonna tell you the answer.

00:02:36.736 --> 00:02:38.087
- [Kelly] Okay.
- Weed gummies.

00:02:38.087 --> 00:02:39.080
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.640
Weed gummies.
(audience laughs and claps)

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.060
- [Tyler] I'm telling you every...

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:45.055
every time you see every it, every-

00:02:45.055 --> 00:02:46.033
- Weed.
- Weed, weed.

00:02:46.033 --> 00:02:48.100
- [Kelly] I love it.
- Every time you see it

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.458
you'll see something else and you go, wow.

00:02:50.458 --> 00:02:51.320
(Kelly laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.280
This movie is so deep!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.450
- It's like watching O in Vegas,

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.860
you see something different every time,

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:58.720
there's so much happening
and you're like, "Wow".

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:01.210
- Wait, you like O too?
- [Kelly] I love O!

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.362
- Did you see it on a gummy?

00:03:02.362 --> 00:03:04.650
- No, I didn't see it on a gummy.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.360
- You like O, I love O,
we gotta get married.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.900
We gotta get married, I'm telling you.

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:10.120
- But it is like, I feel like
you don't even have to be

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:11.917
on a gummy to see O, you
watch O and I'm like,

00:03:11.917 --> 00:03:13.250
I missed that.

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.260
This whole section, like,
the last time I was here

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:16.183
was, 'cause there's so much happening.

00:03:16.183 --> 00:03:18.010
- It's the most incredible
Cirque du Soleil show

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:18.843
I've ever seen.

00:03:18.843 --> 00:03:20.354
Everybody that goes to Vegas,
I'm like, you've gotta see it.

00:03:20.354 --> 00:03:22.420
- It's so good.
- It's really good, yeah.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:23.253
- [Kelly] We're perfect together.

00:03:23.253 --> 00:03:24.086
- Yeah.

00:03:24.086 --> 00:03:25.450
So this one's a bit heavier.

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:28.030
The world seems to be
more and more polarized.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.860
So what do you say to your kids

00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:31.960
when they ask you why
no one can get along?

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.400
This has actually happened to me.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.233
- [Tyler] Really?

00:03:34.233 --> 00:03:35.420
- Yes, about homelessness.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.070
My daughter's very
concerned about homelessness

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:39.650
and she's very concerned
about why people are fighting.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.870
She doesn't understand.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.157
- Especially when Black
Lives Matter was happening

00:03:42.157 --> 00:03:43.737
and the pandemic and everything.

00:03:43.737 --> 00:03:45.973
It's a very hard conversation to navigate,

00:03:45.973 --> 00:03:47.980
what to share or not share yet.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.816
- Yes, exactly.

00:03:48.816 --> 00:03:50.950
Especially at an age where

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:52.840
they're so impressionable with everything.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:55.127
So I've been very, very
careful to try to keep again,

00:03:55.127 --> 00:03:57.710
not having iPads and
not watching television

00:03:57.710 --> 00:03:59.580
and so, you know, monitoring what he sees

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:00.950
has really helped me to not have to

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.220
have that conversation yet.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.650
But it's a really, really hard one,

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:06.140
especially for a black parent
with a little black boy.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.370
- Yeah, it's hard for anybody
to explain to their kid,

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.203
you know, why it's been so bad, but-

00:04:09.203 --> 00:04:10.452
- No, but I've had black
women on this show tell me,

00:04:10.452 --> 00:04:13.210
it's hard for me to explain why

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:15.020
you should be nervous when
you get pulled over by cop.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.290
- Why you should, I've
had these conversations.

00:04:16.290 --> 00:04:18.090
I'm like, oh my God, I've
never had to think about that.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.420
- Yeah, especially when,
when dad has been pulled over

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:22.760
and I was Tyler Perry at the time

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:24.330
and still had a horrible incident.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.830
So it's a scary time but again,

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.457
my hope is that we're raising
people, we're raising kids

00:04:29.457 --> 00:04:32.130
that will come up and
change this and buck all of

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:33.780
- [Kelly] Do better, yeah.
the foolishness, right?

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:35.640
- Yeah, because we've screwed up a lot.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.510
So I'm hoping that this
generation that's coming up,

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:38.970
that we're giving them enough love

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.300
and compassion and teaching
them about humanity.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.909
Not race, but humanity,
love for humanity, right?

00:04:45.909 --> 00:04:47.050
(audience applauds)
And see if that helps.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.690
- It's amazing what the kids are taught.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.390
Like now that I'm a parent, it's amazing.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:53.310
Like, I have a five and seven
year old, they don't know.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.410
They don't even see that,
they're taught that.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.470
And you don't realize it
because we haven't been

00:04:57.470 --> 00:04:58.820
little in a long time, you know?

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:02.854
So, well, not that long,
but like just a minute.

00:05:02.854 --> 00:05:03.687
(Tyler laughs)

00:05:03.687 --> 00:05:04.540
- Just a minute.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.230
- No but, um, but it's
interesting like how,

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:09.910
you know, it is up to us
like, 'cause we teach that.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.320
You teach love, you teach hate.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.530
Like, so it's a... oh, it's
a heavy burden sometimes.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.500
I feel like, so responsible of like,

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.470
am I saying the right thing?

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:18.360
Am I doing the right thing?

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.880
It's very, I don't know.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:20.850
- Let me give you some comfort.

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.200
Every parent who's a good
parent feels that way.

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.610
So you're in, you're in great company.

00:05:24.610 --> 00:05:25.443
We're all trying to figure that out.

00:05:25.443 --> 00:05:26.276
(crowd claps)
- Okay.

00:05:26.276 --> 00:05:27.780
That did make me feel good, thank you.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.740
Like, okay, we're gonna
end on a lighter note.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.573
We're gonna end on a lighter note.

00:05:30.573 --> 00:05:32.480
So is it okay to be competitive

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.300
and not let your kids beat you in games?

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.530
I don't let my kids beat me.

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:37.390
- [Tyler] Me either, nope.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:38.642
- Nope, nope, nope.

00:05:38.642 --> 00:05:41.460
- And my son has this thing he likes to do

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.250
when we're racing, he'll run
in front of me to cut me off

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.200
and I pushed him down and kept running.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.850
He'll get up crying, he's
like why'd you push me down?

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.683
You're cheating!

00:05:49.683 --> 00:05:50.913
You're gonna learn the right way, son.

00:05:50.913 --> 00:05:53.320
- I know, my daughter does
this like when we're swimming,

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:55.000
we'll do laps and she'll
be like, let's race.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.430
And I'm like, I'm really fast, honey.

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:57.720
Like, I'm a lot bigger than you.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.030
And she will try and go, okay one...

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.387
and then she'll jump and
she's supposed to go on three.

00:06:01.387 --> 00:06:02.810
And I'm like, and I'll still beat her

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:03.820
and I'm like, that's right!

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:06.420
- Yeah, that's right, in
your face little girl!

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:08.210
- I'm like, you lost!

00:06:08.210 --> 00:06:09.050
I don't do that.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.650
Um, but I do think it's important.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.410
Like, 'cause I grew up in
Texas and like in Texas,

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:15.480
like sports, they're like,
you have to learn how to lose.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.313
- Yeah.

00:06:16.313 --> 00:06:17.740
- Like you, exactly.
(audience claps)

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.610
Like how many times have you lost in life?

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.530
Even in the entertainment
industry, oh my God.

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:23.760
I've lost so much, like at certain things.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:25.790
You have to learn how
to do that gracefully.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:26.970
- Gracefully, yeah.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.720
My son wasn't having it,
he doesn't like to lose.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.490
- Oh no, neither do
neither one of my children

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.700
and I'm like, if you're
gonna throw a tantrum

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.327
you better get to your room,
I'm gonna chase you there.

00:06:33.327 --> 00:06:35.300
I was like, I can't have that.

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:36.410
Like, you know, whining 'cause you...

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:37.381
I'm like, that's not out a real issue.

00:06:37.381 --> 00:06:38.989
- Nope, no, I don't do that either

